4. Maintained the same mock data and functionality
5. The ProfileSecurity component remains unchanged and will render exactly as it does in the main application
6. Added proper TypeScript support with React.FC type
7. Kept all the existing QueryClient setup

This approach uses React's context system to provide mock data, which is more reliable than trying to modify modules. The component itself remains unchanged and will render with the same appearance and functionality, just with mocked data for preview purposes.

